10
00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:02.770
Ashley?

11
00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.930
Ashley?

12
00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:10.500
Honey. Sweetheart? What are you doing?

13
00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.160
Painting.
- Yeah I know. I think your mom wants some help with the unpacking.

14
00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:19.460
I know.
- So why don't you come outside with me. you can finish your painting later.

15
00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.680
Because I didn't want to move here.
I shouldn't have to carry boxes.

16
00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.290
We had to move here and we all
have to help carry boxes.

17
00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:29.310
Uh-uh. you wanted to move here.

18
00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:32.250
No. I had to move here.
The new story I'm writing is here.

19
00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.540
Why couldn't you just keep writing
in the old house?

20
00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:39.540
Because I was going to have to write college textbooks
to pay for the old house and I can't do that.

21
00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.470
Why not?
- Because I just can't.

22
00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:47.640
But I miss my school.
- Well you know what? The school here is supposed to be pretty good.

23
00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.920
But I want my old one.

24
00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.680
I know. How about this. alright?
I'll tell you what.

25
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.630
If we don't like it here once
I sell my book ...

26
00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:01.310
we'll move back. But only if
we don't like it here.

27
00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.720
Really?
- Really.

28
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.730
You promise?

29
00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:08.000
I promise. But you have to
promise to try to like it here.

30
00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.560
I promise.
- Ok. all right my little artist. what's the number one rule?

31
00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.290
Paint only goes in the bedroom.

32
00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.150
And where doesn't it go?
- Anywhere else in the house.

33
00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.990
Right. Now come with me. we'll move some boxes.

34
00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.740
The sheriff's here.
- Already?

35
00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.590
Be nice this time.
- I'm always nice.

36
00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.770
I'm not kidding. I'm tired of driving 5 miles under the speed limit

37
00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:33.280
only to get ticketed anyway.
Be nice.

38
00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:39.570
Afternoon. Is there a problem?
- No sir. just a friendly visit.

39
00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:43.220
I appreciate that. I'm Ellison Oswalt.
- I know who you are.

40
00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.930
So you're not a fan?
- No.

41
00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:49.370
What can I do for you?

42
00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.400
Not much. I expect. unless I can
convince you to load those boxes ...

43
00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:56.960
back in that truck and leave as soon as you're able.

44
00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:58.700
No. I don't think so.

45
00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.810
But you know what. I do have a couple of extra copies
of 'Kentucky Blood' in my office

46
00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.840
if you want me to get one out and sign it for you. I'll do that.

47
00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.410
No. thanks.

48
00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:09.330
What. is it the writing?
- More a matter of content.

49
00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:13.830
You don't seem to care much for our profession.
- Not everyone in your profession gets it right.

50
00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.080
I've read your books. neither do you.

51
00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.790
Look...

52
00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.500
You got it right with "Kentucky Blood".
I'll give you that.

53
00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:26.810
It's a fine piece of writing. But.
'Cold Denver Morning'. you got it wrong.

54
00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:31.570
It wasn't my fault.
- Your bad theory helped a killer go free.

55
00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:35.190
You ruin people's lives.
This town doesn't need that.

56
00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:40.620
It needs to heal. It needs to forget. And we sure don't want that circus that you bring with you.

57
00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:43.620
Well. there is a missing girl involved here.
- She ain't missing. she's dead.

58
00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.940
Come on. you don't know that.

59
00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:50.520
If that girl is still alive. and it ain't no miracle. then we ain't ever gonna find her.

60
00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:55.340
Well then I guess we should just let it go. huh?
You don't think the town deserves an explanation?

61
00:05:56.110 --> 00:06:00.150
Something like this?
You can never explain something like this.

62
00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:05.710
And if you were able to. the odds are you wouldn't much care for the answer.

63
00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.040
Now. we did our job.
You'll see that.

64
00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:11.830
And this is just another waste of your time. like your last two books.

65
00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:15.990
If writing true crime
has taught me one thing ...

66
00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:19.520
it's that whenever an officer of the law says
I'm wasting my time ...

67
00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:21.940
it just means.
he thinks he's wasting his.

68
00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.850
That's clever. You ought to write that down.

69
00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:30.040
Well. I'm going to go out on a limb and assume that your department is
not my disposal?

70
00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:33.940
Well. what do you know.
You can still get things right on occasion.

71
00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:43.720
Oh. and uh. I find this to be in extremely bad taste.

72
00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.540
What was all that about?
- The usual.

73
00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:59.510
He wanted an autograph.
but he left his copy at home. He'll be back later.

74
00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:02.980
Was it that bad?
Why was he pointing at the house?

75
00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.070
Ellison. we didn't move a few

76
00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:08.780
houses down from a crime scene. again. did we?

77
00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:13.250
Tracy..
No. just don't say anything.
If we did then I don't want to know about it.

78
00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:16.360
We didn't.
- Promise?

79
00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.640
I promise.

80
00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:23.440
Here. make yourself useful.
Kitchen.

81
00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.270
It's going to be good here. all right? You'll see.

82
00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:42.370
You gotta be kidding me.

83
00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.440
"The Family Hanging Out 11 '?

84
00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:54.270
'Barbecue 79'?

85
00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:05.920
I also bought noodles and fortune cookies.
Enjoy it kids.

86
00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:09.430
We're not likely to be eating out much this time.
- Why not?

87
00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.380
You know why.
- I don't.

88
00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:12.790
We haven't sold the old house yet.

89
00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:15.310
Once it's gone.
we'll be able to afford a few extra things.

90
00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.700
Well then sell it already. lower the price if you have to.

91
00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:21.060
We've already lowered it as much as we can without
losing money. The market's terrible.

92
00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.600
Once we're not paying two mortgages
we'll be fine.

93
00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.540
Once I sell my new book. we'll be on easy street.

94
00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.250
Is the story a good story this time?
- Yeah it's good. of course it is.

95
00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:31.710
Will you take me and show me where it happened?
- Trevor.

96
00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.040
Come on. I'm old enough to know about that stuff.
- No. you're not.

97
00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:36.260
Even I'm not old enough to know about that stuff.

98
00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:39.420
Your father writes about terrible terrible things.
and I don't want you knowing anything about that.

99
00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:42.260
You say that like I shouldn't be writing about that.
-That's not what I meant.
That's the way you say it

100
00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:47.750
Well. I'm gonna hear about it in school. anyway. Kids'll hate me again and tell me nonstop about what happened.

101
00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:50.640
Hey. nobody hates you.
- Well. I might as well hear it from you.

102
00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:53.140
Are you listening to this?
- Yes I'm listening.

103
00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:55.220
At least let's make sure that your office stays locked.

104
00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:59.270
It's one thing to hear about it. another thing to see it. I wouldn't want him walking in again. He is 12 years old.

105
00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:02.280
Mom. he knows how old I am.
- Hey. stop it.

106
00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:05.540
What's the first rule?
- Never go in Dad's office.

107
00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.740
And what's your rule?
- Always lock Dad's office.

108
00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:12.960
That's right.
And I don't want to hear another thing about why we're here from anybody.
-Yeah.

109
00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:25.200
You brush your teeth?
- No. not yet.

110
00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:29.970
You're no coming to bed?
- No. I thought I'd set up my office first and get started.

111
00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.190
How long is it gonna be?
- Oh. just an hour or two.

112
00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:35.860
No. I mean.
How long are we here for this time?

113
00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:42.210
Oh. God. I don't know. It could be a long one.
- I liked it better when you were writing fiction.

114
00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:45.680
Nobody likes my fiction.
- Maybe you should try again.

115
00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:50.710
I can't do this without you by my side.
- I'm sorry. I'm on your side.

116
00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.930
I just want to see you enjoying
your work again.

117
00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:59.200
When you're happy.
we are all happy.

118
00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:05.680
I just need another hit. that's all.
Just one more.

119
00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:09.410
What?

120
00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:14.160
You know I'm behind you on this.
- I know. but that's not what you were going to say. what were you going to say?

121
00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:20.300
"Kentucky Blood 'was ten years ago.
- And?

122
00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:26.710
And. what if that was your 15 minutes?
- Ok. what if it was?

123
00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:33.100
If it was. then you can't spend the rest of your life chasing after it.

124
00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:36.540
If you miss out on all the years with the kids. you can't get them back.

125
00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:41.610
I just need one more chance.just one more. I got a really good feeling about this. I really do.

126
00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:45.800
I don't really think I can do this again.
- You're not going to have to .

127
00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:47.990
I mean it.

128
00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:54.940
If this goes sour. like the last time.
I'll take Trevor and Ashley and go back home to my sister.

129
00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.990
Is that fair?
- Yes.

130
00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.700
But it's not gonna go sour.

131
00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:09.710
Give me some love.

132
00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.760
WHERE ARE YOU?

133
00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.790
BOX OF FILMS
HOW DID IT GET THERE?

