00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:47.970
Wake up!

156
00:23:48.130 --> 00:23:51.960
Oh my God. is he okay?
- He's having one of his fits again.

157
00:23:52.120 --> 00:23:55.070
Come outside.
Wake up now.

158
00:23:55.230 --> 00:24:00.450
Wake up.

159
00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:04.010
Look at the stars.

160
00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:11.320
Why are we outside?
- you're good.

161
00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:15.300
You were having a bad dream. just one of those night terrors.
Just go back to sleep.

162
00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:17.790
I thought these were over.

163
00:24:17.860 --> 00:24:21.330
It's just the stress of the move.
I found him in one of the moving boxes.

164
00:24:21.490 --> 00:24:24.920
Poor baby.
- It'll be all right in a few hours.

165
00:24:26.680 --> 00:24:30.540
What is it?
What's the matter?

166
00:24:31.380 --> 00:24:34.540
I want to tell you something.

167
00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.280
I'm just really sorry.

168
00:24:43.240 --> 00:24:48.140
It's not your fault. Come on.
It's cold. Let's go inside.

169
00:24:55.690 --> 00:24:59.400
I was in a box?
-You were in a box.
I don't remember any of that.

170
00:24:59.550 --> 00:25:01.990
Well. it's not the strangest place we ever found you.

171
00:25:02.150 --> 00:25:03.920
Please don't talk about the dryer.

172
00:25:03.920 --> 00:25:07.450
Are we talking about the time we saw Trevor trying to pee in the dryer?

173
00:25:07.620 --> 00:25:10.610
God. Mom. No!
- Sorry. I thought that's what you were talking about.

174
00:25:10.770 --> 00:25:15.200
Did Trevor try to pee in the dryer again?
- Ashley. no. your brother just had a night terror.

175
00:25:15.350 --> 00:25:17.630
Is that like a bad dream?
- Kind of.

176
00:25:17.790 --> 00:25:22.260
Oh. I think I had one of those.
- No. a night terror is a special kind of bad dream.

177
00:25:22.420 --> 00:25:25.290
We would have remembered if you had one... Don't do that!

178
00:25:25.450 --> 00:25:28.920
So. Ashley. you excited about your first day at the new school?

179
00:25:29.840 --> 00:25:31.880
Mmm-hmm.
-What about you?
- I guess.

180
00:25:32.040 --> 00:25:38.040
It's nice to see you're so enthusiastic about our adventure.
- You two. stop it. stop it. Be the bigger person.

181
00:25:39.420 --> 00:25:41.420
You gonna take them?
- Yes. I've got some errands to run.

182
00:25:41.570 --> 00:25:44.280
I think I'm gonna get the lay of the land and let you get some work done.

183
00:25:44.450 --> 00:25:48.900
Eat up kids. you're running late.
- You heard your mother. grab some road breakfast and skedaddle.

184
