201
00:29:53.360 --> 00:29:55.430
Tell him what you drew.
- I drew a tree.

202
00:29:55.620 --> 00:30:00.200
With four people who were hanging from it.
Go to your room. Trevor. I need to speak to your father.

203
00:30:01.020 --> 00:30:05.120
His first day at school. Ellison. and he's already hearing all
the grisly details of your mystery.

204
00:30:05.270 --> 00:30:07.510
What did he hear?
- Exactly what he drew.

205
00:30:07.670 --> 00:30:10.860
Your book is about a family.
who was hung! Christ. Ellison!

206
00:30:11.020 --> 00:30:13.900
Is that all he has heard?
- Is that not enough?

207
00:30:14.290 --> 00:30:17.720
I'm sorry that he had to figure it out like this.

208
00:30:17.880 --> 00:30:22.030
but come on. it was bound to happen.
- That's your response? You think that makes it ok?

209
00:30:22.190 --> 00:30:26.900
No. it doesn't make it ok! Nothing about
what happened to those people is ok.

210
00:30:27.560 --> 00:30:29.980
But bad things happen
to good people. and they ...

211
00:30:29.980 --> 00:30:32.630
still need to have
their story told. They deserve that much.

212
00:30:32.720 --> 00:30:35.980
You're a real man of the people.
- Oh. come on.

213
00:30:41.760 --> 00:30:45.000
I put the kids to bed.
- Kiss them goodnight for me.

214
00:30:45.770 --> 00:30:48.120
You getting good work done?
- Yeah.

215
