00:34:50.960 --> 00:34:54.230
<i> Police have released this photo of
Christopher Miller.</i>

222
00:34:54.340 --> 00:34:57.460
<i> the missing 13 year old son of
William and Penny Miller.</i>

223
00:34:57.650 --> 00:35:01.370
<i> The Millers along with their younger son were found
stabbed inside their home ...</i>

224
00:35:01.480 --> 00:35:05.800
<i> and the police now are asking for any information
that could lead to Christopher's return.</i>

225
00:35:05.870 --> 00:35:08.300
<i> or the apprehension of any suspects involved</i>

226
00:35:08.380 --> 00:35:12.060
<i> in this vicious multiple murder
and child abduction.</i>

227
00:40:09.920 --> 00:40:11.920
No!

228
00:40:34.430 --> 00:40:36.430
The family hanging out.

229
00:40:44.360 --> 00:40:46.520
Pool Party.

230
00:40:52.970 --> 00:40:55.590
Barbecue.

231
00:41:00.500 --> 00:41:03.410
Sleepytime.

232
00:41:33.960 --> 00:41:36.490
Really. I'm fine.
- I'd prefer to take you down to the hospital and have this checked out.

233
00:41:36.560 --> 00:41:39.690
I think you should get stitches.
can't force you. though.

234
00:41:39.770 --> 00:41:42.850
I'm not gonna go.
- Well. the bleeding stopped for now.

235
00:41:43.230 --> 00:41:46.550
but if the bleeding starts again or there's any more swelling.
call a doctor immediately.

236
00:41:46.710 --> 00:41:48.950
Thank you.
I appreciate it.

237
00:41:54.180 --> 00:41:56.180
So. let's go see this hole.

238
00:41:58.430 --> 00:42:03.300
So you say you heard a loud thump and footsteps in the
attic. after the power went out?

239
00:42:05.180 --> 00:42:07.740
Yes.
- But the ladder wasn't down?

240
00:42:08.000 --> 00:42:12.160
No. it wasn't.
- It's not possible to close it from the inside of the attic?

241
00:42:13.400 --> 00:42:15.470
No.
- So. how can an intruder get up there?

242
00:42:15.920 --> 00:42:18.710
I didn't say anyone was up there. I said it just sounded like there was an intruder.

243
00:42:19.220 --> 00:42:22.060
I did see a small snake. though.
- Snakes don't have feet.

244
00:42:24.410 --> 00:42:27.680
No. I'm guessing that you got squirrels.

245
00:42:28.510 --> 00:42:33.150
No way in or out up there.and with all the power gone off in the neighborhood

246
00:42:33.290 --> 00:42:37.360
I bet they got spooked from the sound of everything shutting down at once.

247
00:42:37.680 --> 00:42:40.880
You know how they are.
- Not really. I'm not really a squirrel guy.

248
00:42:43.740 --> 00:42:45.750
I did kill a scorpion. when we first moved in here.

249
00:42:45.800 --> 00:42:47.760
So. maybe I should get an exterminator.

250
00:42:47.760 --> 00:42:51.790
Scorpions have feet. but you wouldn't hear them the way you would squirrels.

251
00:42:54.120 --> 00:42:57.120
Thank you very much. uh.. I will..

252
00:42:58.110 --> 00:43:01.230
Is there anything else I can do for you?
- Actually. there is.

253
00:43:01.500 --> 00:43:04.650
I left my copy of 'Kentucky Blood'
down at the station. It would really mean a lot to me if you signed it.

254
00:43:04.690 --> 00:43:10.260
Of course. I have a few extra copies in my office.
- Thank you so much. that's so great!

255
00:43:11.570 --> 00:43:13.970
Oh. wow. This is like one of those FBI profiler's offices.

256
00:43:14.010 --> 00:43:16.820
I mean. you got a map with pictures connected with yarn and everything. this is crazy!

257
00:43:16.850 --> 00:43:20.720
Deputy. I need you to step outside..No. no. this is my private office. I'm serious

258
00:43:20.750 --> 00:43:23.880
Wait outside.
- Listen. there's. there's a ...

259
00:43:24.050 --> 00:43:26.110
You know there is a page in your book where
you always say nice things ...

260
00:43:26.130 --> 00:43:28.130
about all the people that helped you out?

261
00:43:28.350 --> 00:43:30.670
The acknowledgments??
- Yeah.

262
00:43:30.810 --> 00:43:35.040
And in each one there's always like a line that says. you know like...

263
00:43:35.100 --> 00:43:41.100
"I couldn't have done this without
the tireless efforts of Deputy So-and-So from the local police department...

264
00:43:42.480 --> 00:43:44.680
Right.
- Well. you know. I could be...

265
00:43:46.180 --> 00:43:50.100
like. your Deputy So-and-So. you know I mean. If you don't already have one.

266
00:43:50.260 --> 00:43:53.300
Yeah. are a few things you
could do for me. actually.
-Really?

267
00:43:53.450 --> 00:43:56.470
Yeah. this could be perfect.
Do you have a notepad?

268
00:44:01.000 --> 00:44:04.710
Yes!
- Do you need a pen?
Yes!

269
00:44:05.010 --> 00:44:07.570
I need the street address of a crime.

270
00:44:07.730 --> 00:44:10.280
In 1998. St. Louis. a family was stabbed to death.

271
00:44:10.320 --> 00:44:13.140
They had their throats cut.
It was a pretty ugly affair.

272
00:44:13.320 --> 00:44:16.260
I also need any details you can get me on another murder.

273
00:44:16.290 --> 00:44:20.870
In 1979. a family was burned alive.
parked inside their own car in their own garage.

274
00:44:21.400 --> 00:44:25.070
What city?
- I don't know. all I have is the year and the method of execution.

275
00:44:27.160 --> 00:44:29.130
You think that the two cases
are related?

276
00:44:29.130 --> 00:44:33.100
No. i'm just doing research.
- Ok. I can definitely get this for you.

277
00:44:33.130 --> 00:44:37.070
I gotta wait until the sheriff leaves the office. but I will get it.

278
00:44:37.650 --> 00:44:40.040
Thank you very much. Deputy So-and-So.

279
00:44:44.670 --> 00:44:46.670
I'm sorry
- For what?

280
00:44:46.990 --> 00:44:49.350
I was angry at Trevor today. and I took it out on you.

281
00:44:49.790 --> 00:44:52.380
Don't be sorry.
I know the move's been hard on you.

282
00:44:52.440 --> 00:44:55.720
I'm trying. El. I really am.
- I know.

283
00:44:55.780 --> 00:45:01.780
I just want you here with me. that's all.
- I've always been with you. And I'm with you now.

284
00:45:10.280 --> 00:45:14.160
<i> We're pleased to have Ellison Oswalt on our program tonight. His new book is called."Kentucky Blood '.</i>

285
00:45:14.350 --> 00:45:16.830
<i>It's so good to have you on.
- Thanks for having me. it's a real pleasure.</i>

286
00:45:16.970 --> 00:45:19.850
<i>Man. I got into this.
This is pretty graphic stuff.</i>

287
00:45:20.000 --> 00:45:24.550
<i> So let me start by asking. why do you spend so much time
investigating such grisly content?</i>

288
00:45:25.030 --> 00:45:27.860
<i> Fame and money?
No. I'm just kidding.</i>

289
00:45:28.020 --> 00:45:32.570
<i>The honest answer is that. I'm really driven by a sense of injustice.</i>

290
00:45:32.740 --> 00:45:35.220
<i> You know. when I think about the awful things that happen to these people ...</i>

291
00:45:35.250 --> 00:45:38.530
<i> and that those responsible
were never even identified. let alone caught.</i>

292
00:45:38.700 --> 00:45:42.150
<i> I knew when I started this particular case that I
might stumble on a few things</i>

293
00:45:42.150 --> 00:45:44.020
<i> that maybe someone might
have overlooked.</i>

294
00:45:44.020 --> 00:45:49.270
<i>MIGHT stumble? No. you in fact DID uncover some additional information that the cops had overlooked.</i>

295
00:45:49.390 --> 00:45:55.390
<i> Well. look. first off. let me say that there are a lot of good police officers out there. and I don't want to in any way disparage what they do. all right?</i>

296
00:45:56.080 --> 00:45:59.440
<i>But the police work. getting something wrong. means
ruining people's lives.</i>

297
00:45:59.590 --> 00:46:01.590
<i> And good crime writing can
set things right.</i>

298
00:46:01.970 --> 00:46:05.660
<i> So ultimately. what feels better?
Seeing justice done ...</i>

299
00:46:05.700 --> 00:46:10.650
<i> or seeing your book "Kentucky Blood " number one on the New York Times bestseller list?</i>

300
00:46:10.910 --> 00:46:15.750
<i> The justice.
Without question.</i>

301
00:46:15.790 --> 00:46:20.280
<i> I'd rather cut my hands off than
write a book for fame or money.</i>

302
00:48:53.780 --> 00:48:55.860
Are you making Daddy his coffee?
- Yes.

303
00:48:55.890 --> 00:49:00.490
Can I help? I want to bring it to him.
- Sure. honey. but we have to make it just right.

304
00:49:00.780 --> 00:49:03.020
He is very particular about his coffee.

305
00:49:16.310 --> 00:49:19.670
I brought you your coffee. Daddy.
- Thank you. sweetheart.

306
00:49:25.110 --> 00:49:28.350
Hello. Mr Oswalt?
- Hey. Deputy So-and-So.
- Hey listen. I'm sorry to get back to you so late today

307
00:49:28.520 --> 00:49:30.930
I couldn't make the calls from the office.You know. the sheriff.

308
00:49:30.950 --> 00:49:34.010
Yeah. I understand.
- But. I got what you asked about.

309
00:49:34.090 --> 00:49:38.830
There was a Martinez family in Sacramento. California that died in their garage in 1979.

310
00:49:38.950 --> 00:49:42.380
Their car was set on fire.
And one of their sons was 9 years old. they never found him.

311
00:49:42.530 --> 00:49:47.440
Do you have the street address?
- Yes. 8224 Billington in Sacramento.

312
00:49:47.590 --> 00:49:48.690
What about St. Louis?

313
00:49:48.690 --> 00:49:54.290
The address of the house where the Miller murders occurred is 2976 Piedmont Way St. Louis.

314
00:49:54.800 --> 00:49:59.040
That is excellent! All right. 29 ...
Wait. did you say 2-9-7-6? Like 29-76?

315
00:49:59.120 --> 00:50:03.590
Yeah. what? Does that mean something to you?
- Uh. no.no. it doesn't. Thank you. thank you. Deputy.

316
00:50:07.410 --> 00:50:12.300
Before the Stevensons moved here. they lived where the Miller family murders happened. Holy shit!

317
00:53:54.090 --> 00:53:57.910
Oh God! Is he ok?
- I found him outside.

318
00:53:58.070 --> 00:54:00.540
We have to put a lock on his door.
It's way worse than it was.

319
00:54:00.690 --> 00:54:02.690
I'll call the doctor in the morning.

320
00:54:07.020 --> 00:54:09.920
All right now. you stay with him.
I left something outside.

321
00:54:32.630 --> 00:54:34.860
Good dog.

322
00:54:35.020 --> 00:54:38.390
Good dog.
I don't wanna hurt you.

323
00:54:41.930 --> 00:54:45.010
I just wanna get my bat.

324
00:54:45.860 --> 00:54:49.530
So if you come at me I'm gonna bash your head in.

325
00:54:50.610 --> 00:54:53.170
That's fine. you keep it.

326
00:55:02.420 --> 00:55:05.360
You ok?
- Yeah. I'm fine. Come on.

327
00:55:06.890 --> 00:55:10.710
Trevor is too old to still be having these.
He's supposed to have outgrown them by now.

328
00:55:10.870 --> 00:55:13.990
Oh. he's all right.
- Just stop.

329
00:55:14.450 --> 00:55:16.790
Stop what?
- Drop the book.

330
00:55:17.740 --> 00:55:22.580
Look. we can pack up. get out of town. and never look back.
- Why? Because he's having some night terrors?

331
00:55:22.620 --> 00:55:25.900
No. it's more than that.
He's never been this bad.

332
00:55:26.060 --> 00:55:28.920
You've never been this bad. You've been at this book less than a week and you're already a mess!

333
00:55:29.080 --> 00:55:31.390
You never crack into the whiskey this early.

334
00:55:31.910 --> 00:55:36.280
So now you're saying I'm a drunk?
- No. I'm saying there's something you're not telling me.

335
00:55:36.440 --> 00:55:39.660
Something that's eating you up. and whatever it is.it seems to be getting to Trevor as well.

336
00:55:39.820 --> 00:55:42.360
Something's different.
- Yeah something's different. Do you wanna know what it is?

337
00:55:42.530 --> 00:55:44.920
How much do you wanna know?
- I want to know why you're different.

338
00:55:44.950 --> 00:55:48.230
Something is different because I have never been onto something this big before.

339
00:55:48.390 --> 00:55:50.900
Do you remember how it was when I was writing 'Kentucky'? Do you remember that?

340
00:55:51.060 --> 00:55:53.320
Well this is much bigger than that! Much!

341
00:55:54.180 --> 00:55:57.010
I'm talking about a potentially important work. here!

342
00:55:57.160 --> 00:56:00.500
I'm talking about a mega hit.
This could be my " In Cold Blood"!

343
00:56:00.660 --> 00:56:05.160
A movie deal. talk shows. right? A national book award.

344
00:56:05.320 --> 00:56:08.860
And more money than.. we could live on it forever if we wanted to.
- I don't care about any of that!

345
00:56:09.010 --> 00:56:12.550
Yes you do! Everybody does!
This is my shot. Tracy!

346
00:56:14.230 --> 00:56:17.840
What?
- I'm just worried about you.

347
00:56:18.010 --> 00:56:21.700
Well. don't be. Nothing is wrong.

348
00:56:21.860 --> 00:56:24.530
Then why did you come in white as a ghost?

349
00:56:25.480 --> 00:56:28.060
Because I saw a dog.

350
00:56:28.230 --> 00:56:32.080
A dog?
- A very big dog.

351
00:56:32.240 --> 00:56:35.220
Like Cujo. baby. I had never seen him before.

352
00:56:35.380 --> 00:56:37.330
Is he gone?
- Yeah. he's gone.

353
00:56:37.330 --> 00:56:42.180
I just need a little more time.
I promise it's worth it.

354
00:56:43.420 --> 00:56:47.790
Every minute that we're here. we are a minute closer
to the happy ending that we always dreamed of.

355
00:56:47.950 --> 00:56:49.950
We're almost there.

356
00:56:56.900 --> 00:57:00.120
Deputy.
- Mr Oswalt. these came in this morning.

357
00:57:00.150 --> 00:57:03.340
I had a few of the pertinent files pulled for you and had them faxed over.

358
00:57:03.500 --> 00:57:06.600
Really? Thanks.
- No problem.

359
00:57:07.430 --> 00:57:10.300
You think I could come in for a second?

360
00:57:11.770 --> 00:57:15.030
Yeah. sure.
- Thanks.

361
00:57:15.550 --> 00:57:20.640
Look. I know what you must think of me. some small-town deputy...

362
00:57:20.800 --> 00:57:23.980
that's starstruck with the famous writer. but I'm not some local moron.

363
00:57:24.140 --> 00:57:27.160
I didn't say that you were.. you know...

364
00:57:27.320 --> 00:57:31.380
I have a degree in criminology
and I've taken my fair share of forensic science courses.

365
00:57:33.530 --> 00:57:37.710
I also know a series of connected murder cases when I see one. Mr Oswalt.

366
00:57:37.860 --> 00:57:40.690
Look. listen. we missed something. I get that.

367
00:57:40.840 --> 00:57:44.400
But if you want me to run interference for you while you get this worked out.

368
00:57:44.440 --> 00:57:47.640
I gotta be in the loop. Just. a little bit.

369
00:57:49.080 --> 00:57:51.080
You really want to help?

370
00:57:51.110 --> 00:57:55.350
It's my home. Mr Oswalt.
What happened here. happened to all of us.

371
00:57:56.680 --> 00:57:58.990
All right. come here.

372
00:58:07.880 --> 00:58:11.220
Who is that?
- I don't know.

373
00:58:11.380 --> 00:58:13.380
That's what I'm hoping to find out.

374
00:58:16.000 --> 00:58:20.890
You think that these are serial murders?
- Maybe. More ritualized than necessarily serial.

375
00:58:21.050 --> 00:58:23.610
They're really spread out.
Not just regionally but over time.

376
00:58:23.630 --> 00:58:26.370
The first one I found dates back to the 60s.

377
00:58:26.530 --> 00:58:29.600
The 1960s?
- Yeah.

378
00:58:30.310 --> 00:58:34.010
Wait. that would put the guy. what. in his 70s?
- Or his 60s.

379
00:58:34.170 --> 00:58:37.390
Yeah. I don't know.
- Look at the methodology.

380
00:58:37.550 --> 00:58:40.890
In the toxicology reports.. in some cases the killer drugged his victims.

381
00:58:41.050 --> 00:58:44.430
Wait. with what?
- Well. they couldn't tell for sure.

382
00:58:45.190 --> 00:58:48.800
But by drugging them. the killer removes his need to overpower them.

383
00:58:48.960 --> 00:58:51.290
Here it is the tree branch that did the heavy lifting.

384
00:58:51.320 --> 00:58:53.100
In Sacramento. he lit a family on fire.

385
00:58:53.100 --> 00:58:56.720
In St. Louis he slit their throats.
The first family. he drowned.

386
00:58:56.880 --> 00:59:00.180
Drowning? You never said anything about anyone being drowned.

387
00:59:00.340 --> 00:59:02.530
The only other significant link
between the murder cases is that

388
00:59:02.680 --> 00:59:06.820
in each instance. the killer murdered the entire family. except one.

389
00:59:06.980 --> 00:59:09.080
A child. which he took with him.

390
00:59:09.170 --> 00:59:14.960
That. and this symbol appears in several of the crime scenes.

391
00:59:14.990 --> 00:59:17.480
That looks like something from out of the occult.

392
00:59:17.640 --> 00:59:20.860
Look. you might wanna call the university.

393
00:59:21.020 --> 00:59:24.520
There is a professor. over there. Professor Jonas. He's an occult crime expert.

394
00:59:24.670 --> 00:59:28.590
and the state police bring him in on some of the weirder stuff.

395
00:59:29.010 --> 00:59:31.010
I think this qualifies.

396
00:59:31.880 --> 00:59:35.770
So where do you think that drowning happened?
- That's what I need you to find out.

397
01:01:55.620 --> 01:01:57.600
Professor Jonas?
-Yes.

398
01:01:57.600 --> 01:02:00.850
Hey. thank you for getting back to me so quickly. I appreciate that.

399
01:02:01.760 --> 01:02:05.460
Of course. I'm a really big fan.
I'm flattered that you would even...
-Thanks.

400
01:02:05.620 --> 01:02:09.530
When I saw the photos that you had sent to me. I knew exactly what cases that you were studying.

401
01:02:09.560 --> 01:02:11.750
How would you know what cases I was looking at?

402
01:02:11.910 --> 01:02:16.280
The symbol that you sent me.
isn't a pentagram.

403
01:02:16.440 --> 01:02:20.340
It's not something that you would see teenagers or a
Norwegian black metal band ...

404
01:02:20.500 --> 01:02:23.120
paint on the wall in goat's blood

405
01:02:23.280 --> 01:02:27.500
to be edgy. or to piss off the Christians.
No. this is a bit more obscure than that.

406
01:02:27.660 --> 01:02:31.280
I know.. that one from the hallway.

407
01:02:31.440 --> 01:02:35.050
That's from the late nineties
in St. Louis.

408
01:02:35.220 --> 01:02:40.260
The other one. the car hood. that
is from Sacramento. that's about 30 years ago.

409
01:02:40.430 --> 01:02:42.510
Tell me about the one in Sacramento.

410
01:02:42.570 --> 01:02:46.470
It's a symbol associated
with the worship of a pagan deity.

411
01:02:46.630 --> 01:02:48.420
A pagan deity? What kind of deity?

412
01:02:48.420 --> 01:02:52.320
A very obscure one. dating back to Babylonian times.

413
01:02:52.480 --> 01:02:56.890
Named Bughuul. The eater of children.
- Did you say. 'eater'?

414
01:02:57.440 --> 01:03:01.220
Yes. uh. of children.
Thank you. Jessica.

415
01:03:01.380 --> 01:03:07.380
The crimes that you're dealing with. they all have the element of a missing child. correct?
- Yes. that's correct.

416
01:03:08.220 --> 01:03:11.040
Well. Bughuul eats the children.

417
01:03:11.590 --> 01:03:16.320
Now. the fragments of stories that have survived. they all revolve around him

418
01:03:16.480 --> 01:03:19.470
eating the souls of children. to survive.

419
01:03:19.620 --> 01:03:24.830
Now each story involves a different way that he lures

420
01:03:24.990 --> 01:03:28.830
or tricks these children away from the physical world

421
01:03:28.870 --> 01:03:31.750
and traps them in his own netherworld.

422
01:03:31.910 --> 01:03:34.930
where he consumes their souls over time.

423
01:03:35.090 --> 01:03:38.990
Now. any worship of this deity would include blood sacrifice ...

424
01:03:39.150 --> 01:03:42.290
or the wholesale eating of the child.

425
01:03:42.450 --> 01:03:46.110
So you're saying the person who made these symbols is eating children?

426
01:03:46.940 --> 01:03:52.510
Well. that would fit the stories.
Of course. the few times that this symbol has shown up ...

427
01:03:52.670 --> 01:03:55.890
none of the crimes have been related in any way to any of this.

428
01:03:56.370 --> 01:03:59.150
So this might be more
of a cult initiation ...

429
01:03:59.310 --> 01:04:03.010
rather than the actual actions of any one man.

430
01:04:06.430 --> 01:04:08.890
There's been another one. hasn't there?

431
01:04:11.960 --> 01:04:16.530
I think so. yes.
- Tell me everything you can.

432
01:09:51.840 --> 01:09:56.640
So. I appreciate you coming by.
- Yeah. that's not a problem at all.

433
01:09:56.670 --> 01:10:01.010
So. we're becoming friends. right?
- It suppose. yeah.

434
01:10:01.130 --> 01:10:03.400
I mean. I can trust you. right?
- Absolutely.

435
01:10:04.990 --> 01:10:09.080
So if I were to ask you something in earnest. you wouldn't read too much into it?

436
01:10:14.000 --> 01:10:20.000
Was there anything weird about the Stevensons?

437
01:10:23.840 --> 01:10:27.210
No complaints from them about anything... strange?

438
01:10:29.700 --> 01:10:34.750
No. not to my knowledge.
- The investigators. they didn't notice anything odd or inexplicable about the house?

439
01:10:34.790 --> 01:10:38.180
Any weird stories?
- No.

440
01:10:38.470 --> 01:10:43.400
Mr Oswalt. is there something you want to tell me?

441
01:10:47.340 --> 01:10:50.650
Ok. look. clearly something happened and you want
talk to somebody about it. right?

442
01:10:51.570 --> 01:10:54.320
Ok. well does your wife know about it?

443
01:10:59.090 --> 01:11:03.400
Wait. did she know whose house this is... was?

444
01:11:09.380 --> 01:11:13.430
Oh man. that is a conversation I would not want to be around for!
- Me neither.

445
01:11:13.470 --> 01:11:19.470
I'm sorry. so. what? You saw some thing weird. heard something spooky in the house?

446
01:11:22.050 --> 01:11:26.350
Yes. precisely.
- What exactly?

447
01:11:28.570 --> 01:11:34.570
I don't believe in any.. you know. stuff.
- By stuff. you mean ...

448
01:11:34.820 --> 01:11:39.810
supernatural. metaphysical.
paranormal. that type of stuff?

449
01:11:39.990 --> 01:11:43.130
Right. of course you don't.

450
01:11:43.170 --> 01:11:45.170
You would have never moved into a crime scene if you did. so..

451
01:11:45.200 --> 01:11:48.490
here we are. having this conversation.

452
01:11:49.580 --> 01:11:55.580
But. there was none of that with the Stevensons. huh?

453
01:11:56.830 --> 01:12:00.920
No. in the short amount of time that the Stevensons lived here. they never called the police ...

454
01:12:00.950 --> 01:12:05.410
and never have the police called on them or reported anything bizarre that came up in the investigation.

455
01:12:06.320 --> 01:12:09.210
Want to know what I think?
- Yes.

456
01:12:11.220 --> 01:12:16.180
I think you have moved yourself into
the house of murder victims ...

457
01:12:16.210 --> 01:12:19.370
and set about immediately trying to put yourself in their headspace.

458
01:12:19.370 --> 01:12:23.110
I also think that you've  begun discovering things
on this case  ...

459
01:12:23.110 --> 01:12:25.720
that go to darker places than you were prepared for.

460
01:12:26.610 --> 01:12:31.460
I also think that every time I come to your house. there's a whiskey bottlein your office.

461
01:12:32.890 --> 01:12:37.840
Mr. Oswalt. I'm not saying that you
have a drinking problem.

462
01:12:37.970 --> 01:12:38.850
I don't think that.

463
01:12:38.850 --> 01:12:42.870
Nor do I think that you're making any of this up to get attention.

464
01:12:43.380 --> 01:12:47.420
I don't think that. What I do think is that you are under so much stress ...

465
01:12:47.450 --> 01:12:51.930
You put yourself under so much stress that your mind is trying to process all of it at once.

466
01:12:53.480 --> 01:12:57.670
So you don't believe any of that... otherwordly stuff?

467
01:12:57.670 --> 01:13:01.760
Are you kidding me?
I believe in all that stuff.

468
01:13:01.760 --> 01:13:07.310
I wouldn't sleep one night in this place. are you nuts? Four people were hung by their necks ...

469
01:13:07.310 --> 01:13:11.250
in a tree in your backyard.
And that little girl. God knows. where... God knows what..

470
01:13:12.120 --> 01:13:15.350
I'm sorry. you know what?

471
01:13:15.350 --> 01:13:18.850
You should try to get out more. Mr Oswalt. Try to clear your head.

472
01:13:19.960 --> 01:13:23.630
Total honesty?

473
01:13:24.440 --> 01:13:28.250
Last night I thought ...

474
01:13:28.250 --> 01:13:31.550
that something was in the house.

475
01:13:31.550 --> 01:13:33.950
And then I woke up on the couch

476
01:13:33.950 --> 01:13:36.740
holding a baseball bat.

477
01:13:38.970 --> 01:13:43.540
I guess if I thought something was in my home at night.
I would be a little bit freaked out. too.

478
01:13:43.540 --> 01:13:48.440
But. listen to me. Mr Oswalt. If you sleep in this house ...

479
01:13:48.440 --> 01:13:50.770
it's just gonna do terrible things to your head.

480
01:13:58.240 --> 01:14:00.540
What's going on?
- Your daughter apparently thought

481
01:14:00.570 --> 01:14:03.300
there wasn't enough room on her walls for her new painting.

482
01:14:03.980 --> 01:14:07.610
Ashley!
-No. that's not it!
- We talked about it! I only gave you one rule ...

483
01:14:07.620 --> 01:14:10.950
it was a big deal for us to let you paint on your wall. What was it? What's the rule. Ashley?

484
01:14:10.950 --> 01:14:14.040
Paint only goes in the bedroom.
- What makes you think you could paint out here?

485
01:14:14.040 --> 01:14:19.240
I wanted to paint her picture. but she didn't want it in my room.
because that used to be her brother's room

486
01:14:19.240 --> 01:14:22.490
What? Who are you talking about?

487
01:14:22.490 --> 01:14:24.850
Stephanie.
- Who is Stephanie?

488
01:14:24.850 --> 01:14:29.100
She used to live here. She's the one Daddy's writing his book about.

489
01:14:34.420 --> 01:14:37.190
Ashley. go to your room and shut the door.

490
01:14:45.030 --> 01:14:48.830
What the hell were you thinking?
Did you think I wouldn't find out?

491
01:14:48.830 --> 01:14:51.570
Of course I knew you
were gonna find out. eventually. ok?

492
01:14:51.570 --> 01:14:55.560
But don't blame me for not telling you. because remember. you never wanted to know.

493
01:14:55.560 --> 01:14:59.600
Don't try and pin this on me!
I asked you! I asked you if we were living in that house.

494
01:14:59.600 --> 01:15:03.880
You asked me if we were living two houses down from
a crime scene. I said. no.

495
01:15:03.880 --> 01:15:06.840
We never should have come here!
- Nobody died here.

496
01:15:06.870 --> 01:15:11.570
It's not like we're sleeping where somebody was killed! It's not like they had to wipe the blood off the walls!

497
01:15:11.610 --> 01:15:13.420
So you're saying it didn't happen here?
- No.

498
01:15:13.420 --> 01:15:18.460
It happened in the backyard.
- Oh. that is so.. and you think that makes a difference?

499
01:15:18.490 --> 01:15:22.870
No Ellison. it doesn't.You have done some crazy shit in the past..

500
01:15:22.870 --> 01:15:27.260
but this really takes the cake.
What on earth possessed you to move here?

501
01:15:27.260 --> 01:15:29.380
We've never been this broke before.
- That's no excuse.

502
01:15:29.380 --> 01:15:32.490
This came on the market and was a steal ...
- Gee. I wonder why.

503
01:15:33.420 --> 01:15:36.880
So. what Trevor drew last week.
that happened here?

504
01:15:39.380 --> 01:15:43.390
The previous owners of this home were hung from a tree in our backyard?

505
01:15:44.710 --> 01:15:48.580
That is so sick. Ellison. And you let our little girl play back there?

506
01:15:48.580 --> 01:15:51.980
Why shouldn't I?
- Our son is having night terrors ...

507
01:15:51.980 --> 01:15:54.190
and drawing pictures of this crime at school

508
01:15:54.190 --> 01:15:56.660
and our daughter just painted a little dead girl on our walls.

509
01:15:56.660 --> 01:16:01.480
Technically. she's missing.
- I don't want to hear about technicalities!

510
01:16:01.480 --> 01:16:05.540
Do you understand what you've done this time? The kind of jeopardy you put your children in?

511
01:16:05.540 --> 01:16:07.850
Your marriage?
- Yes. I understand.

512
01:16:07.850 --> 01:16:10.800
I see. Is there anything you won't do for your goddamn book!?

513
01:16:13.720 --> 01:16:17.230
Apparently not.
I guess this is all worth it to you.

514
01:16:17.230 --> 01:16:19.190
What is it worth?
- Putting your family at risk.

515
01:16:19.190 --> 01:16:21.300
Risk of what? Of more paintings?
- Don't! Your daughter...

516
01:16:21.300 --> 01:16:24.930
My daughter has a father who loves her. that is always around.

517
01:16:24.930 --> 01:16:28.470
who encourages her to be herself.
The worst thing that ever happened to her ...

518
01:16:28.470 --> 01:16:31.570
is one time. she moved into a house
where a family was killed ...

519
01:16:31.570 --> 01:16:34.570
she found out about the murders.
she felt sorry for that little girl ...

520
01:16:34.570 --> 01:16:36.730
So she painted a fucking picture!

521
01:16:36.730 --> 01:16:39.810
That's what she does. that's what she always has done.

522
01:16:39.810 --> 01:16:43.830
What else do you want from me?

523
01:16:43.830 --> 01:16:46.550
How about a home where we feel safe?

524
01:16:46.550 --> 01:16:49.030
How about neighbors who don't hate us ...

525
01:16:49.040 --> 01:16:52.380
a town where I can buy groceries
without getting strange looks?

526
01:16:52.420 --> 01:16:55.500
How about a life that doesn't involve our kids...

527
01:16:55.500 --> 01:16:59.270
drawing or painting the sick details of some horrific tragedy ...

528
01:16:59.270 --> 01:17:03.600
or working out their deep-seated anxieties by doing bizarre shit in the middle of the night.

529
01:17:03.600 --> 01:17:09.070
How about that? Would that be ok?
- I can give all that to you as soon as the book is finished!

530
01:17:09.070 --> 01:17:11.450
This book isn't for us. it's for you.

531
01:17:11.450 --> 01:17:13.870
Don't say that. It's not true.
- It IS true.

532
01:17:13.870 --> 01:17:16.400
There are plenty of other ways
you can provide for this family.

533
01:17:16.430 --> 01:17:19.020
Doing what?!
Teaching?

534
01:17:19.020 --> 01:17:21.730
Editing journalism textbooks?

535
01:17:21.850 --> 01:17:24.140
Don't you understand?

536
01:17:24.140 --> 01:17:27.380
That writing is what gives my life meaning.

537
01:17:27.380 --> 01:17:31.040
These books are my legacy.

538
01:17:32.910 --> 01:17:36.920
I have always supported you doing what you love

539
01:17:37.700 --> 01:17:41.440
But writing isn't the meaning of your life.

540
01:17:41.440 --> 01:17:45.720
You and me. right here. this marriage.
that's the meaning of your life.

541
01:17:45.720 --> 01:17:49.790
And your legacy?
That's Ashley and Trevor.

542
01:17:49.820 --> 01:17:52.530
Your kids are your legacy.

543
01:18:05.160 --> 01:18:07.970
Did I get Daddy in trouble?
- No. sweetie.

544
01:18:08.580 --> 01:18:12.610
Your daddy got Daddy in trouble.
- I'm sorry I painted on the wall.

545
01:18:12.610 --> 01:18:16.910
I know.
Get a good night's sleep.

546
01:21:09.950 --> 01:21:12.590
What is happening?

547
01:23:00.010 --> 01:23:03.050
One. two. three. four ...

548
01:23:03.050 --> 01:23:07.220
five. six. seven. eight ...

549
01:23:26.910 --> 01:23:29.960
Three. four. five. six ...

550
01:23:29.960 --> 01:23:33.670
seven. eight. nine. ten.
- What the hell are you doing?

551
01:23:33.670 --> 01:23:35.670
We have to leave here.

552
01:23:36.100 --> 01:23:39.020
What's the matter? What's happened?
- You were right.

553
01:23:39.910 --> 01:23:44.250
I made a mistake.
We should have never come to this house.

554
01:23:45.180 --> 01:23:47.910
We have to leave now.

555
01:23:48.070 --> 01:23:51.520
You're freaking me out.
- Get the kids and pack the car.

556
01:23:51.680 --> 01:23:56.180
We have to leave.
Go!!!

557
01:24:39.700 --> 01:24:42.410
Honey. slow down.
- I just want to get to the highway.

558
01:24:42.440 --> 01:24:46.670
I want to put as much road between us and this town as we can.

559
01:24:47.350 --> 01:24:50.750
Where are we going. Daddy?
- We're going home. honey.

560
01:24:50.790 --> 01:24:54.160
Our home? Like you promised?
- Yeah. like I promised.

561
01:24:54.800 --> 01:24:58.400
What about our stuff?
- We're going to call the movers in the morning. all right?

562
01:25:13.950 --> 01:25:16.460
It's ok.

563
01:25:25.840 --> 01:25:29.290
Evening. Oswalts.
- Sheriff.

564
01:25:29.450 --> 01:25:33.440
License and registration.

565
01:25:36.140 --> 01:25:39.700
Driving pretty fast for this time of night. don't you think?

566
01:25:39.860 --> 01:25:42.220
Anything I oughta know about?

567
01:25:42.700 --> 01:25:46.270
Just trying to take your advice. that's all.
- Which advice would that be?

568
01:25:47.270 --> 01:25:49.270
Leave town and never look back.

569
01:25:55.880 --> 01:25:59.170
You weren't bullied away. were you?
- I'm sorry?

570
01:25:59.330 --> 01:26:04.400
I don't wanna be reading in your book that angry townsfolks chased you out of here.

571
01:26:05.110 --> 01:26:09.520
If you've been mistreated. I wanna know about it.
- There isn't gonna be any book.

572
01:26:10.200 --> 01:26:14.010
No book?
- No. sir.

573
01:26:19.200 --> 01:26:23.670
Well then. I don't see any reason for me to have your autograph.

574
01:26:24.770 --> 01:26:28.900
One more favor?
Hold it under 60 until you cross the county line?

575
01:26:29.060 --> 01:26:31.660
Then you're somebody else's problem.

576
01:26:33.380 --> 01:26:37.470
Yes. sir.
- Did you mean that?

577
01:26:37.990 --> 01:26:40.730
About the Book?
Yes.

578
01:26:41.640 --> 01:26:45.230
Promise?
- I promise.

579
01:26:48.900 --> 01:26:52.130
Let's go home.

580
01:27:07.490 --> 01:27:09.770
That goes in the office.
over there on the right.

581
01:27:13.510 --> 01:27:16.090
$10 says that Trevor
sleeps through the night.

582
01:27:16.130 --> 01:27:18.560
No. I'm not taking that bet.

583
01:27:47.910 --> 01:27:49.910
THREE SCANNED IMAGES FOR YOU

584
01:28:08.910 --> 01:28:10.780
Mr Oswalt! I'm sorry that it took so long to get back to you.

585
01:28:10.780 --> 01:28:12.520
There's been so little written about Bughuul ...

586
01:28:12.520 --> 01:28:15.670
that no one has actually bothered to scan this material before.

587
01:28:15.700 --> 01:28:17.740
Well. what am I looking at?

588
01:28:17.770 --> 01:28:22.940
You're looking at an engraving. an old sketch from the Dark Ages. and fragments of a deteriorated fresco.

589
01:28:22.980 --> 01:28:25.740
There just isn't a lot left.
Everything else has been destroyed.

590
01:28:25.740 --> 01:28:27.480
Why?
- Superstition.

591
01:28:27.480 --> 01:28:31.080
Early Christians believed that
Bughuul actually lived in the images themselves...

592
01:28:31.110 --> 01:28:34.180
and that they were gateways into his realm.

593
01:28:35.360 --> 01:28:37.240
Gateways?
- Yes. the ancient church believed

594
01:28:37.240 --> 01:28:40.570
that he would take possession of those who saw the images ...

595
01:28:40.600 --> 01:28:43.540
and cause them to do terrible things.

596
01:28:43.690 --> 01:28:47.780
Or in some cases. he could even abduct the viewer into the images themselves

597
01:28:47.950 --> 01:28:51.510
Children exposed to the images
were especially vulnerable to

598
01:28:51.670 --> 01:28:55.200
to Bughuul's possession and/or abduction.

599
01:28:55.460 --> 01:28:58.540
What if you destroyed him?
- Sorry. I don't follow.

600
01:28:58.700 --> 01:29:02.230
If you destroyed the images..with a fire. what would happen then?

601
01:29:02.390 --> 01:29:05.440
Do you mean literally. or in the stories?

602
01:29:05.600 --> 01:29:09.800
In the stories. if an image was destroyed. then the gateway would be closed ...

603
01:29:09.970 --> 01:29:13.890
and Bughuul would no longer have access to this world. right?

604
01:29:14.050 --> 01:29:19.140
Mr Oswalt. what kind of book are you writing. exactly?

605
01:29:21.460 --> 01:29:25.390
I don't know.
I'm not even sure I have a book anymore.

606
01:29:25.550 --> 01:29:28.560
But. thank you for your time.
- Anytime.

607
01:29:44.030 --> 01:29:46.030
DEPUTY SO-AND-SO

608
01:31:32.060 --> 01:31:34.280
DEPUTY SO-AND-SO

609
01:31:35.270 --> 01:31:39.270
Do you know what time it is?
- Yeah. I know. I'm sorry. but I've been trying to call you all day.

610
01:31:39.440 --> 01:31:41.800
What's the problem?
- Ok. the problem is that you moved.

611
01:31:42.420 --> 01:31:46.500
How is that a problem?
- I was compiling all the data that you've had me collecting

612
01:31:46.660 --> 01:31:51.030
and once I started putting it together in a nice readable package. I saw the connection. It was obvious.

613
01:31:51.190 --> 01:31:53.790
What was it?
- The dates! The addresses!

614
01:31:53.830 --> 01:31:59.040
Each family that you had me look up had previously lived in the house where one of the earlier murders took place.

615
01:31:59.840 --> 01:32:02.930
Each family? All five of them?
- Yes.

616
01:32:03.090 --> 01:32:05.210
When you put them in chronological order ...

617
01:32:05.220 --> 01:32:08.100
you can actually draw a line from murder to murder to murder.

618
01:32:08.890 --> 01:32:14.390
We knew that the Stevensons previously lived in the same
St. Louis house where the Millers had their throats cut.

619
01:32:14.550 --> 01:32:18.110
But. before the Miller family was killed. the Millers lived in the same house in Orange County ...

620
01:32:18.280 --> 01:32:20.440
where the De Luzio lawn massacre occurred.

621
01:32:20.600 --> 01:32:23.520
Guess where the Luzio's lived
before they moved to Orange County?

622
01:32:23.680 --> 01:32:26.770
In Sacramento. where the  Martinez family was
burned to death in their garage.

623
01:32:26.930 --> 01:32:30.820
Exactly. The pattern goes back to 1966 Oregon drownings.

624
01:32:30.980 --> 01:32:33.900
Listen Mr Oswalt. you just moved out of the last house in line!

625
01:32:34.060 --> 01:32:39.110
If this guy is still out there. you not only just sped up his timeline.
you put yourself in it!

626
01:32:40.830 --> 01:32:43.110
Thanks. Deputy.

627
01:33:22.430 --> 01:33:24.910
Stephanie.

628
01:33:43.260 --> 01:33:45.260
It's the missing kids.

629
01:34:53.510 --> 01:34:55.510
Goodnight. DADDY

630
01:35:04.650 --> 01:35:08.820
I like that you made the movies longer. They're better this way.

631
01:35:53.850 --> 01:35:57.870
Don't worry. Daddy.
I'll make you famous again.

632
01:35:58.000 --> 01:36:01.110
Best watched using Open Subtitles MKV Player
